---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../../components/PageHeader.astro';
import ScoreCard from '../../components/ScoreCard.astro';
import MetaScoreBadge from '../../components/MetaScoreBadge.astro';
import VerdictBox from '../../components/VerdictBox.astro';
import CTA from '../../components/CTA.astro';
import DisclosureBlock from '../../components/DisclosureBlock.astro';
import LastVerified from '../../components/LastVerified.astro';
import FAQ from '../../components/FAQ.astro';
import { appBySlug } from '../../data/apps';
import { SITE } from '../../data/site';

const app = appBySlug('flowkey');
const title = 'How Much Does Flowkey Cost in 2026? Full Price Breakdown';
const description =
  'Flowkey costs $20/month or $120/year (7-day free trial, card required). Full breakdown of every plan, the discount reality, and how it compares to Simply Piano, Skoove, and Pianote.';
---

<BaseLayout title={`${title} | ${SITE.name}`} description={description}>
  <PageHeader title={title} crumbs={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'How much does Flowkey cost?' }]}>
    Flowkey costs <strong>$20/month</strong> or <strong>$120/year</strong> on the annual plan,
    with a 7-day free trial (card required). It is the best price-for-ratings value in the category —
    the highest-rated app we track (MetaScore <MetaScoreBadge app={app} showSources={false} />) at the
    lowest annual price. Full breakdown below.
    <ScoreCard app={app} linkReview slot="aside" />
  </PageHeader>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="prose">
    <h2>Flowkey prices in 2026</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Monthly:</strong> $20/month — the flexible option, but the worst value: $240/year if you stay on it.</li>
      <li><strong>Annual:</strong> $120/year — $10/month-equivalent, and the plan almost every committed learner picks.</li>
      <li><strong>Free trial:</strong> 7 days, card required. Cancel before day 7 to avoid being charged.</li>
      <li><strong>No permanent free tier.</strong> After the trial ends, you pay or lose access.</li>
      <li><strong>Run by Yamaha.</strong> Flowkey is a Yamaha company — the app is backed by one of the largest instrument makers in the world, so your subscription is not funding a fragile startup.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>The monthly vs. annual math</h2>
    <p>
      The break-even is fast: 6 × $20 = $120, exactly the annual price. If you will practice for more
      than 6 months, the annual plan is cheaper than month-to-month. Committed learners should buy
      the year; casual tinkerers should start on the trial and reassess.
    </p>
    <h2>The discount reality: the sticker price is a ceiling</h2>
    <p>
      Flowkey's "real" price is whatever the current discount is. The app runs frequent promotions and
      third-party discount sales (StackSocial-style deals have been a long-running pattern) — the $120/yr
      sticker price is a ceiling, not a floor. Check our <a href="/deals/">deals page</a> before buying;
      you may never need to pay full price.
    </p>
    <h2>Flowkey vs. competitor prices</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Simply Piano:</strong> $150/yr — $30 more than Flowkey, and rated lower (MetaScore 8.6 vs 8.9). You pay extra for a more structured beginner curriculum.</li>
      <li><strong>Skoove:</strong> $150/yr — same price as Simply Piano, with real-instructor support bundled.</li>
      <li><strong>Yousician:</strong> $140/yr — covers piano plus guitar, ukulele, bass, and singing, but its piano curriculum is shallower.</li>
      <li><strong>Piano Marvel:</strong> $120/yr — the same sticker price as Flowkey, MIDI-focused, but a smaller user base and lower ratings.</li>
      <li><strong>Pianote:</strong> $240/yr — double Flowkey's price, for real teachers, live Q&amp;A, and a genuine advanced path.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Context: $120/year is roughly one-twenty-fifth the cost of a year of weekly private piano lessons. Every app here is cheap next to a teacher — the real question is which app you will actually open.</p>
    <h2>Hidden costs and things to watch</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Auto-renewal</strong> after the trial: the card you enter on day 1 gets charged on day 8 unless you cancel.</li>
      <li><strong>Advanced players hit a ceiling.</strong> The lesson path runs out quickly for serious players — if that is you, you are buying a $120 stepping stone, not a multi-year tool. <a href="/pianote-review/">Pianote</a> is the honest upgrade path.</li>
      <li><strong>Course depth for absolute beginners.</strong> Flowkey's song-first approach is its strength, but the course structure is thinner than Simply Piano's for day-one beginners.</li>
      <li><strong>Keyboard costs extra.</strong> Like every app here, Flowkey assumes you have a piano or keyboard — mic input works with any instrument, no cable needed, but you still need the instrument.</li>
    </ul>
    <VerdictBox title="Is the price fair?">
      At $120/yr, Flowkey is the best value in the category on paper: the highest MetaScore (8.9) at the
      lowest mainstream annual price. It only fails the value test for advanced players who will outgrow
      the curriculum. Full verdict: <a href="/is-flowkey-worth-it/">is Flowkey worth it in 2026?</a>
    </VerdictBox>
    <CTA app={app} label="Try Flowkey free for 7 days" />
    <p>More: <a href="/flowkey-review/">full Flowkey review</a> · <a href="/simply-piano-vs-flowkey/">Simply Piano vs Flowkey</a> · <a href="/flowkey-vs-pianote/">Flowkey vs Pianote</a> · <a href="/flowkey-alternatives/">alternatives</a></p>
    <FAQ items={[
      { q: 'How much is Flowkey per month?', a: '$20/month on the monthly plan, or $120/year ($10/month-equivalent) on the annual plan.' },
      { q: 'How much is Flowkey per year?', a: '$120/year at sticker price — but Flowkey runs frequent promotions, so check the deals page before buying; you may never need to pay full price.' },
      { q: 'Is there a Flowkey free trial?', a: 'Yes — 7 days, card required. Cancel before day 7 to avoid being charged. There is no permanent free tier.' },
      { q: 'Is Flowkey cheaper than Simply Piano?', a: 'Yes — Flowkey costs $120/yr vs Simply Piano\u2019s $150/yr, and Flowkey carries the higher MetaScore (8.9 vs 8.6).' },
      { q: 'Can I use Flowkey on my phone and computer?', a: 'Yes — one subscription covers iOS, Android, and Web, and it works with mic or MIDI input on all of them. You still need your own piano or keyboard.' },
    ]} />
    <DisclosureBlock />
    <LastVerified />
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
